# Explicit `ycolumns` with default `series`: the default skips the y column and keeps
# the remaining string columns; the other numeric column `n` is left out of the chart.
mode: run
---- query
from '../../data/orders.csv'
| where customerId == "c-042"
| summarize revenue = sum(amount), n = count() by customerId, month = startofmonth(timestamp)
| extend label = "x"
| sort by month asc
| render timechart with (ycolumns = revenue)
---- expected
customerId | month                | revenue | n    | label
string     | datetime             | real    | long | string
-----------+----------------------+---------+------+-------
c-042      | 2023-12-01T00:00:00Z |  523.75 |    3 | x
c-042      | 2024-01-01T00:00:00Z |  185.0  |    1 | x
c-042      | 2024-02-01T00:00:00Z |  451.25 |    2 | x
c-042      | 2024-03-01T00:00:00Z |   90.5  |    1 | x
render: timechart x=month y=[revenue] series=[customerId, label]
